  "id": "COMPOUND:5778 - PROTEIN:813",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Aniline and the Kappa-type opioid receptor, as it is indirectly linked through multiple pathways. Aniline is identified as a target of several compounds, including 5-hydroxytryptamine receptor 2C, which in turn is a target of Ginkgolide A and 3-Methylfentanyl. All of these compounds have been shown to interact with the Kappa-type opioid receptor, indicating a possible mechanism of action involving the receptor. The scores from the paths suggest a consistent and strong relationship, but the exact nature of the interaction remains to be determined. The evidence supports a possible role for Aniline in modulating the Kappa-type opioid receptor, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm this relationship.",
